WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.000
In May 2018,
the European Commission put forward

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.200
a proposal
for the next EU's long-term budget.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.040
The proposal is a result
of open debate with citizens,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.040
beneficiaries of EU funding,

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.600
Members of the European
and national Parliaments,

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.000
representatives of EU member states.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.200
We have conducted
a rigorous examination of all policies

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.560
and proposed an ambitious but balanced
budget: one that is fair for all.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.360
Investing more than ever in research,
innovation and the digital sector

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.400
means investing in Europe's future.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.160
Our next programmes for research,
innovation and for digital projects,

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.360
will allow our Union
to bridge the current investment gap,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.720
become a front-runner
in market-creating innovation

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.480
and capture
the real value of the data economy.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.280
How will we do this?
By working together.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.520
Because together we are stronger
and can achieve more!

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.880
The EU Regional and Cohesion policy
will keep reducing economic

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.760
and social disparities
between countries and regions.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.840
It will be simpler and more flexible,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.880
to be able to adapt easily to new
priorities and better protect citizens.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.400
The budget for the youth programme
Erasmus+ will be doubled

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.480
to enable more young people
across Europe to study.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.120
This would give them more opportunities.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.960
Every euro that we invest in Erasmus
is an investment in our future.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.520
With relatively modest amounts,
the EU budget will continue mobilizing

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.560
public and private investments
throughout Europe...

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.600
... supporting economic growth
and job creation.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.080
The Investment Plan for Europe
has proven a success

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.000
when it comes to mobilizing
private investment and creating jobs.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.120
With InvestEU,
we are taking this successful model

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.520
and expanding it across the many
EU financing programmes on offer.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.840
We are simplifying,
doing more with less,

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.640
and placing a stronger focus
on social investments.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.320
A modernised Common Agricultural
Policy that ensures safe quality food

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.960
and fairness
for the farmers who produce it.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.280
This means support for sustainability,
environmental initiatives,

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.280
innovation in farming
and developing vibrant rural areas.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.200
A greater share of the EU budget
than ever before

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.240
will be devoted to protect the
environment and fight climate change.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.200
With an increase of funding
of almost 60% for LIFE programme,

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.440
the EU budget can contribute
to protecting our environment

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.240
and speeding up the transition
to a clean, energy-efficient,

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.880
low-carbon
and climate-resilient economy.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.320
Investments in security and defence
will be significantly boosted

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.080
so that Europe can effectively respond

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.800
...and protect EU citizens,
their values and way of life.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.160
No Member State can meet
these challenges on its own.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.680
That is why the EU steps up its role
in security and defence.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.760
The European Defence Fund
will support cross-border investments

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.520
in areas needed
to protect our citizens -

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.000
for example encrypted software
and drone technology.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.400
The EU budget for border and migration
management will be almost tripled...

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.160
to make
the EU’s external borders stronger,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.760
to make migration policy fairer
and more realistic,

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.520
and to improve internal security

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.280
More funding will be available
to promote peace and stability,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.000
to defend the EU’s interests
in the world...

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.040
...and provide development assistance
and humanitarian aid,

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:03.520
with flexibility for a faster response
to new crises and challenges.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.800
With the United Kingdom
leaving the Union,

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.560
there will be only 27 countries
contributing to the budget...

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.400
...while the EU citizens still want
a Europe that is prosperous

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:20.120
and sustainable, safe and secure,
stronger on the global scene.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.440
The Commission proposes
a modern long-term budget,

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.800
aligned to its political priorities,
fit to deliver,

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.200
and focused on the EU added value.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.840
A Europe, that takes greater
responsibility for its citizens,

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.040
needs resources
that match its ambitions.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.680
The EU’s long-term budget,
proposed by the Commission,

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:46.360
can enter into force only when approved
by all of member states in the Council

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.920
and with the consent
of the European Parliament.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.000
And time really matters:

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.640
- to allow for the new programmes
to start on 1 January 2021

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.840
- to give certainty to authorities,
partners and beneficiaries of EU funding

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.920
- to keep the momentum
of the economic recovery

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.680
and show that the EU
is united and ready to deliver.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.360
A budget for a Union the Protects,
Empowers and Defends

